From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 09:47:08 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: keep the CPU DAI name across component rebind

The Qualcomm machine driver parses its CPU link directly instead of
using snd_soc_of_get_dai_link_cpus(). Its name can still point into
memory owned by a component which may unbind before the card.

Use the managed lookup for the CPU link. Keep the parsed arguments
available for the existing link ID selection.

Codex verified the ARM64 Qualcomm machine helper and its link to the
new ASoC core export.

Link: https://github.com/torvalds/linux/commit/33a130f6ed8c75ed59b12889a417a57fb80d0abf
Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/common.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/common.c b/sound/soc/qcom/common.c
index d9f256d51..f84be0689 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/common.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/common.c
@@ -262,7 +262,7 @@ int qcom_snd_parse_of(struct snd_soc_card *card)
 			return -EINVAL;
 		}
 
-		ret = snd_soc_of_get_dlc(cpu, &args, link->cpus, 0);
+		ret = devm_snd_soc_of_get_dlc(dev, cpu, &args, link->cpus, 0);
 		if (ret) {
 			dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
 				      "%s: error getting cpu dai name\n", link->name);
-- 
